														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-271363">
									

<p>Giving it Keter-like properties would be a bit of a plot hole, would it not? Given that it existed as a mathematical concept, unstored on any medium, long before anyone actually constructed it.</p>
<p>Rather, I think it's pretty clear that it's far better to keep something like this lying around contained; as a mathematical concept, <em>anyone</em> could rediscover it at any time (as indicated by the trailing memo), and there is a certain necessity that we study the properties of broken arithmetical systems for future comparison with any other similar SCPs that require containment.</p>

