<p>Very very necro posting here, but just a few things to point out.<br />
Firstly, I searched for this Penrose online, but I found nothing about a proof of one plus one is two.<br />
Secondly, the said proof isn't valid in the first place. As in, there is no need to prove it, as 2 IS DEFINED to be 1+1. We do not prove a definition.</p>
<p>This can counter what PlasmaFox had said: we use the number as it is because we defined them to be that way, not the other way round.</p>

